WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.550 --> 00:00:03.710
The DARPA Grand Challenge
is a competition

00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:05.630
for autonomous
vehicles sponsored

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:07.580
by the Department of Defense.

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:09.830
The vehicles must be
able to navigate a course

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:14.180
and avoid unexpected obstacles
all without human interaction.

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:17.750
The 2007 competition will
take place in an urban setting

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:20.060
with vehicles having
to obey driving laws

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:21.860
and deal with traffic.

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:24.290
For the first time,
MIT in collaboration

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:26.450
with Olin College and
the Draper Laboratory

00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:28.450
is entering the grand challenge.

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:32.270
MIT's entry uses a combination
of lasers, cameras, and radar

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:35.270
to perceive its surroundings
and detect obstacles.

00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:37.910
Its software then uses the
data from those sensors

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:39.710
to determine the
safest way to proceed.

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:11.940
When the vehicle encounters
an obstacle in the roadway,

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:20.690
the car stops, backs up, and
examines its surroundings,

00:01:20.690 --> 00:01:23.290
and then plots a new course
to safely maneuver around

00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:24.960
the obstacle.

